  "id": "trade-please-campaign",
  "name": "Trade Please Campaign",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Trade Please campaign (とりかえっこプリーズ) ran from 10 February to 31 July 1998 with CD and video releases, among them Trade Please by Suzukisan, a unit of Imakuni?, Sachiko Kobayashi and Raymond Johnson. Players mailed the form from one of those releases with two of their own cards and a return envelope, and got two cards back: the Trade Please! trainer, drawn by Imakuni?, and, by the course they chose, Charizard, Blastoise or Venusaur, each the Base Set Pokémon in new art by Ken Sugimori. The three are cosmos holos with the Pikachu Records logo in place of a set symbol, and came again, unchanged, with the Pokémon Song Best Collection CD in January 1999. In 2016, for the Pokémon Card Game's 20th anniversary, Pokémon Centers and Pokémon Stores ran the Trade Please Campaign 20th, swapping Charizard and the Trade Please! card, now a Supporter, for 20 cards with the original card back.",
